{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794229261,"nonce":"ywJa0atXhwtpTneWEWZA83UcWOo=","message":"Landed on `roadmap-493a53c-integration` (4d89a2a..191a534).\n\n**Changes**\n- src/theme/mod.rs: added `accent_soft` token to Tokens, LIGHT (0xdfd2ed) and DARK (0x332d3c); added a WCAG contrast unit test for both palettes\n- src/theme/style.rs: replaced `pill_active` with `chip_selected` (accent_soft fill, 1px accent border, accent text) and `chip_unselected` (transparent, 1px border, text_muted); added `nav_bar` (3px accent marker) and `icon_accent`\n- src/ui/components.rs: `toggle_chip(label, selected, multi, on_press)` shows a leading `lu::check()` when selected and multi; active `top_pill` uses `chip_selected`; added `card_grid` built on `responsive`, plus `grid_columns` and a test\n- src/ui/screen.rs: Overview uses `card_grid` with min width 380 and gap 16, and `overview_card` is now `Fill` width; Kind chips are multi, status/state/epic chips are not; sidebar active item gets a 3px accent bar (fixed 22px, row centered)\n- docs/design.md: documented the selected-state rule and `card_grid`\n\n**Gates:** tests ok · clippy ok · fmt ok\n**Review:** 0 findings — 0 auto, 0 by hand, 0 deferred\n\n**Decisions**\n- The contrast test passes through the border, not the fill. Accent vs panel is about 4.9:1 in light and 8.5:1 in dark. `accent_soft` vs panel is only about 1.2:1. The task's \"(or border)\" wording allows this. The test also checks that the accent label on `accent_soft` is at least 3:1.\n- The 1280px and 2560px criterion was checked by layout math, not visually. The overview grid is roughly 2 columns at 1280 and 5 at 2560. The app was not launched.\n- `card_grid` takes `(items, min_width, gap, render)` rather than prebuilt elements, because the `responsive` closure rebuilds elements on every resize and `Element` is not `Clone`.\n- The sidebar bar is a separate fixed 22px container in a centered row, because a `Fill`-height bar would spread the nav items over the sidebar.\n- Repositories page and the other card lists already use `Fill` width, so `card_grid` is only used on Overview.\n- `pill_active` was removed, since it had no other users and would fail `clippy -D warnings`.","files":null}]}